| What building and trialing 10.11.21.1001 (bob) taught us. R22 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:86-88): "the seated 05 for each page should explain what you learned". Every line names its source; nothing here is new law.
|
| - Face 01 (brand cards bob and cats) passed TRIAL-K2 and was seated at blob 5415cef2 under R2 and R20 (commit 42ffbc9), while face 00 stays a draft (R14).
| - R15 removed the bob and cats 04 face; a compute test still expected it and failed (docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md finding 20; crates/compute/tests/http.rs:261), routed to COMPUTE.
| - The seqpage check disagrees with the kernel face 00: check.seq on the exported page flags "stamp state draft disagrees with the page's entries (live)" and "seat-01: is not a registry field for type general" (docs/BUILD-LOG.md [APP] round 3). That is QUESTIONS Q31, Q34 and Q38 showing up in a real page.
| - TRIAL-K3 (docs/trial/kernel-trial-3.md, finding 14) reports the same stamp-state clash from the trial side and raised it as Q40.

